# K03 NS-ROLES-1b (Codex K03-S5-ALIAS-VISIBILITY-20261007-07 Q1, K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# :666, :722): for absent b, `b: tick` with tick a method binds b to tick's whole occurrence -- no wrapper, nothing
# runs at the binding; `b: args` and `b(args)` call tick, with its signature, on the occurrence b holds.
# At the root: got takes b(3), tick's result.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: ticks 0
fn: tick (int: n) int
    node\ticks: node\ticks + n
    return: n + 1
end: tick
int: got 0
b: tick
got: b(3)
fn: m () int
    if: got != 4 || node\ticks != 3
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
